  "scope": "S1 summary and S2 explicit-/16 workaround NIC route-selection cut. 32 hub-probe route facts plus 3 S1 spoke next-hop dependency facts. Not a complete hybrid or stateful forwarding replay.",
  "dateContext": "Feature-registration request is 2026-10-22T11:20:47Z. NIC text outputs lack capture timestamps, exact commands and API versions; S1/S2 names and report establish scenario order, not an atomic snapshot.",
  "reconstruction": [
    "All ten observed spoke prefixes, local hub prefixes, NVA next-hop address and rt-gw summary/explicit route sets retained. rt-gw is associated to both GatewaySubnet and snet-hub-probe.",
    "Subnets and directional gateway-transit flags come from the deployment script and report; no native all-resource S1 dump is present. Script reflects later S4 too, so later SD-WAN/ER additions are not mixed into this cut.",
    "rt-spoke1 contains only its two S1 observed UDRs with BGP propagation disabled; no unobserved route-table associations on other spokes are invented.",
    "One logical BGP VPN branch retains the observed /16 context. Native LNG connected host /32 and its public-IP next-hop representation are not modeled/asserted, and the fixture does not certify complete VPN RIB equivalence.",
    "The later rt-nva SD-WAN UDR and ER/SD-WAN branches are outside the S1/S2 cut; no preview disablePeeringRoute control is enabled."
  ],
  "exclusions": [
    "Preview suppression was rejected as UnauthorizedClientApplication and registration remained Pending. No Azure-validated preview behavior.",
    "Only selected independent NIC prefix/source/active/next-hop facts are compared; not entire tables or public VPN next-hop IP equality.",
    "Stateful NVA counters and actual session outcomes remain archived context, not validated conntrack/firewall emulation. No forwarding certification for this cut.",
    "Later S4 three-hybrid ER/VPN/SD-WAN BGP and packet-path assertions are still queued, not completed by these two exports.",
    "Cloud/account/provider IDs, public management addresses and credentials are omitted. No live resources queried or changed."
  ],
